// THE DEATH TOKEN (Corey, 2026-10-08) - the Wilderness Slayer currency, and this server's own.
//
// A random drop from a kill made ON A SLAYER TASK, IN THE WILDERNESS (area_wilderness/scripts/
// death_token.rs2), spent at the Undertaker in Edgeville and nowhere else.
//
// UNTRADEABLE, deliberately. An untradeable currency that buys tradeable goods is a gold laundry
// with extra steps: the shop's prices become the trading post's prices and the token stops meaning
// anything. Untradeable also means nobody can farm them for somebody else, and the only way to hold
// one is to have stood in the Wilderness and killed something you were told to kill.
//
// THE MODEL is this build's own: a procedural fourteen-sided coin with the cache's skull struck
// into its face in shallow relief, merged into one mesh (the technique gentradingpostmodel.py uses).
//
// THE MESH LIES FLAT, which is a model decision and not a camera one: the world draws a dropped
// item with the model exactly as it was built, so a disc standing in the x/y plane lands on its
// edge like a dropped wheel. It also RESTS ON y=0 rather than straddling it, because the icon
// camera aims at model.minY / 2 on the assumption that a model stands on the ground - a mesh
// centred on the origin renders low in the slot, which is what the first one did.
//
// So 2dxan is the camera looking DOWN at a coin on the floor, not along at a coin facing you. 445
// of 2048 is about 78 degrees: near enough overhead to read the skull, shallow enough to keep a
// sliver of the near rim and with it the sense that the thing has a thickness. Tuned against the
// real inventory render (tools/models/ObjIconRender.java --mode 0, a pack slot and not a cert's
// 1.5x) beside coins, bones and a tinderbox for scale.
[death_token]
name=Death token
desc=Struck from the plateau's own black stone. Someone died for this.
model=obj_death_token
2dzoom=1150
2dxan=445
2dyan=0
2dxof=0
2dyof=0
stackable=yes
cost=120
members=no
tradeable=no
